0 / np.pi\nx = np.arctan2(yy, xx) * 180 / np.pi\n\n# Limit to be further north than 70 degrees latitude\nx = x[y > 70]\ny = y[y > 70]\n\n# Set depth to be -10 metres\nz = np.ones_like(x) * (-10.0)","key":"XWNCZcX9Kt"},{"type":"outputs","id":"7p3kn5m2ulTAgNlRzvgKb","children":[],"key":"l8G9mdmeLy"}],"key":"sYUnGeW9uw"},{"type":"block","kind":"notebook-content","children":[{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":1,"column":1},"end":{"line":1,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Next, we will consider the timing of the simulation. The ASTE data used here begins on 1st February 2002, so this must be the starting time, ","position":{"start":{"line":1,"column":1},"end":{"line":1,"column":1}},"key":"yIqIAnOkNQ"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"t","key":"TaqZEQOQdJ"},{"type":"text","value":". However, this dataset is a snapshot, and does not have a true time dimension.","position":{"start":{"line":1,"column":1},"end":{"line":1,"column":1}},"key":"e8XILR6p4U"}],"key":"oofdUUV6F3"}],"key":"ndqiev2sQb"},{"type":"block","kind":"notebook-content","children":[{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":1,"column":1},"end":{"line":1,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"We will also need to choose for how long we would like to simulate our particles. Because the dataset has no true time dimension, we must think of time relatively rather than absolutely. Let’s choose to simulate these particles forwards in time for six months, such that the end time is ","position":{"start":{"line":1,"column":1},"end":{"line":1,"column":1}},"key":"jxBjqNL5rv"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"2002-08-01","key":"KlRcFWejnj"},{"type":"text","value":". This means that the particles will move about for six months using the velocities stored in ","position":{"start":{"line":1,"column":1},"end":{"line":1,"column":1}},"key":"vptNpbonNs"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ds","key":"l0qsoMi9xq"},{"type":"text","value":".","position":{"start":{"line":1,"column":1},"end":{"line":1,"